		<UML:TaggedValue tag="id" xmi.id="EAID_5527012A_DAE6_478C_8FA8_8E0AEFECD631" value="OR041" modelElement="EAID_DDCB7CBA_48DF_4AE2_99D7_197CBC35B5A9"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="text" xmi.id="EAID_FB349EB4_5B10_422A_8C22_D4D4FC53B584" value="&lt;memo&gt;#NOTES#[Source requirement] For the&#xA;seawater cooling system, if a main&#xA;circulation pump-related&#xA;configuration is adopted, a low&#xA;supply condition shall be capable&#xA;of alarming to facilitate timely&#xA;startup or switching." modelElement="EAID_DDCB7CBA_48DF_4AE2_99D7_197CBC35B5A9"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="id" xmi.id="EAID_C713076A_4728_42C0_B98B_99E8DFFE24A7" value="OR041.1" modelElement="EAID_6B6311B8_C7ED_4F19_BBBC_D56DB40C947B"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="text" xmi.id="EAID_03B60F1A_C8D4_471A_BB3B_8FFB32CEE6E2" value="&lt;memo&gt;#NOTES#When the seawater cooling system&#xA;is configured with a main&#xA;circulation pump, a low supply&#xA;alarm function shall be provided.&#xA;The alarm signal shall be capable&#xA;of being displayed on the bridge&#xA;or at the main control station so&#xA;that operators can promptly start&#xA;the standby pump or switch to the&#xA;standby pump. (criterion:&#xA;{{TBD|unit:MPa|ref:S43 ABS Marine&#xA;Vessel Rules Part 4&#xA;2021|component:Seawater cooling&#xA;system main circulation&#xA;pump|intent:Low supply alarm&#xA;threshold|hint:The alarm threshold&#xA;shall be determined based on the&#xA;manufacturer&#x27;s technical data or&#xA;project calculation documents, and&#xA;shall not exceed the specific&#xA;manufacturer, model, and control&#xA;system configuration scope}};&#xA;grade: C; derivation: Deferred;&#xA;route: OPEN_ITEM)" modelElement="EAID_6B6311B8_C7ED_4F19_BBBC_D56DB40C947B"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="id" xmi.id="EAID_6892B0B1_B183_44B6_99A9_4FB5919628D4" value="OR041.2" modelElement="EAID_DDB62B1E_D2B3_4D35_B78F_B3B0E6759EB6"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="text" xmi.id="EAID_01E394FF_887E_4AF7_A7F6_7D32625A0B61" value="&lt;memo&gt;#NOTES#The seawater cooling system shall&#xA;be provided with at least two&#xA;cooling water pumps, one of which&#xA;shall be a standby pump. The&#xA;capacity of the standby pump shall&#xA;not be less than the capacity of&#xA;the main pump, and at least one&#xA;pump shall be driven by an&#xA;independent drive unit.&#xA;(criterion:&#xA;{{TBD|unit:unit|ref:S44 PRS Ship&#xA;Machinery Piping&#xA;Systems|component:Seawater cooling&#xA;water pump|intent:Number of pumps&#xA;and standby pump capacity|hint:At&#xA;least two pumps, one of which is a&#xA;standby pump; standby pump&#xA;capacity not less than main pump&#xA;capacity; at least one pump&#xA;independently driven}}; grade: C;&#xA;derivation: Deferred; route:&#xA;OPEN_ITEM)" modelElement="EAID_DDB62B1E_D2B3_4D35_B78F_B3B0E6759EB6"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="id" xmi.id="EAID_B9D114CF_EAAB_4E99_AB94_35E9BACC3945" value="OR041.3" modelElement="EAID_95E42999_8855_4A18_AE75_FA82AEFAB546"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="text" xmi.id="EAID_51B0004F_1E14_4F50_B310_A5F7FD97D206" value="&lt;memo&gt;#NOTES#After the seawater cooling system&#xA;low supply alarm is triggered, the&#xA;standby pump shall be capable of&#xA;being started automatically or&#xA;manually, or switching to the&#xA;standby pump shall be possible, to&#xA;restore the cooling water supply.&#xA;(criterion: {{TBD|unit:s|ref:S28&#xA;Wärtsilä 32 Product Guide, Cooling&#xA;Water System|component:Seawater&#xA;cooling system main circulation&#xA;pump|intent:Standby pump startup&#xA;or switching response&#xA;time|hint:The response time shall&#xA;be determined based on the&#xA;manufacturer&#x27;s technical data or&#xA;project calculation documents, and&#xA;shall not exceed the specific&#xA;manufacturer, model, and control&#xA;system configuration scope}};&#xA;grade: C; derivation: Deferred;&#xA;route: OPEN_ITEM)" modelElement="EAID_95E42999_8855_4A18_AE75_FA82AEFAB546"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="id" xmi.id="EAID_9B1F0C50_3B21_41B2_907B_39ECE27905B9" value="OR041.4" modelElement="EAID_6CE9721C_3D07_439B_ABC2_445B8C7E50B7"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="text" xmi.id="EAID_9B86FD33_E61E_4502_A600_D8C0C0D73579" value="&lt;memo&gt;#NOTES#The sensor for the seawater&#xA;cooling system low supply alarm&#xA;shall be provided independently&#xA;and shall be capable of&#xA;continuously monitoring the&#xA;seawater cooling water supply&#xA;pressure or flow rate. The alarm&#xA;signal shall be transmitted to the&#xA;engine control system or alarm&#xA;monitoring system. (criterion:&#xA;{{TBD|unit:MPa|ref:S21 Caterpillar&#xA;Cooling Systems Application and&#xA;Installation&#xA;Guide|component:Seawater cooling&#xA;water pressure switch|intent:Low&#xA;supply alarm trigger&#xA;pressure|hint:The alarm trigger&#xA;pressure shall be determined based&#xA;on the manufacturer&#x27;s technical&#xA;data or project calculation&#xA;documents, and shall not exceed&#xA;the specific manufacturer, model,&#xA;and control system configuration&#xA;scope}}; grade: C; derivation:&#xA;Deferred; route: OPEN_ITEM)" modelElement="EAID_6CE9721C_3D07_439B_ABC2_445B8C7E50B7"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="id" xmi.id="EAID_53CC06C7_24B7_484B_99D3_E84D55920B3F" value="OR041.5" modelElement="EAID_020B2954_DAF2_4777_BC5E_EE2D271C7B70"/>
		<UML:TaggedValue tag="text" xmi.id="EAID_017266FB_6ADD_47ED_9394_28E39ED629C0" value="&lt;memo&gt;#NOTES#The threshold and action logic of&#xA;the seawater cooling system low&#xA;supply alarm shall be strictly&#xA;limited to the corresponding&#xA;manufacturer, model, and control&#xA;system configuration scope, and&#xA;shall not be generalized beyond&#xA;that scope. (criterion:&#xA;{{TBD|unit:MPa|ref:S43 ABS Marine&#xA;Vessel Rules Part 4&#xA;2021|component:Seawater cooling&#xA;system main circulation&#xA;pump|intent:Low supply alarm&#xA;threshold|hint:The alarm threshold&#xA;shall be determined based on the&#xA;manufacturer&#x27;s technical data or&#xA;project calculation documents, and&#xA;shall not exceed the specific&#xA;manufacturer, model, and control&#xA;system configuration scope}};&#xA;grade: C; derivation: Deferred;&#xA;route: OPEN_ITEM)" modelElement="EAID_020B2954_DAF2_4777_BC5E_EE2D271C7B70"/>
